    "text": "I'm a developer building a chrome extension. I set this in my background script: chrome.runtime.onMessageExternal.addListener(\n(request, sender, sendResponse) => {\nif (request.accessToken) {\nchrome.storage.local.set({ accessToken: request.accessToken });\nchrome.storage.session.set({ accessToken: request.accessToken });\nsendResponse({ success: true, message: \"Token has been received\" });\n}\n}\n);\n\nAnd I have this in my content script:\n\nuseEffect(() => {\nconst listener = () => {\nconsole.log(\"Access token changed\");\nchrome.storage.session.get([\"accessToken\"], (result) => {\nif (!CheckTokenExpiry(result.accessToken)) {\nconsole.log(\"Access token saved:\", result.accessToken);\nprops.setOnboarding(false);\n}\n});\n};\n\nchrome.storage.onChanged.addListener(listener);\nreturn () => {\n  chrome.storage.onChanged.removeListener(listener);\n};\n}, []);\n\nBut the listener event is never firing even when I was able to log access token saved. What am I doing wrong?"
  }
]
